From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Do not name the event dispatcher thread

Some process-protection modules terminate Wine-Wayland's event reader after
identifying its diagnostic thread description.  The process then keeps
rendering, but never receives the compositor's initial xdg_surface configure
and no native window can be mapped.

The description has no functional purpose.  Leave the helper unnamed so it
cannot be singled out while preserving the existing event-loop behavior.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
@@ -29,9 +29,6 @@ WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(waylanddrv);
 
 static DWORD WINAPI wayland_read_events_thread(void *arg)
 {
-    const THREAD_NAME_INFORMATION info = {RTL_CONSTANT_STRING(L"winewayland_dispatcher")};
-    NtSetInformationThread(GetCurrentThread(), ThreadNameInformation, &info, sizeof(info));
-
     WAYLANDDRV_UNIX_CALL(read_events, NULL);
     /* This thread terminates only if an unrecoverable error occurred
      * during event reading (e.g., the connection to the Wayland
-- 
